A||||3||Zoom88||How TO (help)........remove side panel and molding.||||5||
Z||000000||Zoom88||11-23-2001||12:02 PM|||| I recieved my side scoops from Dave and I am ready to install. Can anyone PLEEZE give me detailed instruction on how to remove the panel and molding so I can try and keep from damaging any thing. Plus I have some Sail Panels coming in that I will be replacing any help instruction on there replacement would be greatly appreciated. This is on my 88 Formula. Thanks !!!<BR> Hope everyone had a great Thanksgiving !!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||11-23-2001||12:11 PM||||Not sure about the your first topic, but if you got the sail panels from "Paul Mckibben"<BR>he has detailed insructions on his website.<P>I just installed some on my 88 Formula from him. I just used a razor knife to scrape the underside of sailpanel, then you have to basically break up the old panel and remove it in pieces.<P>------------------<BR>1988 Formula <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (red & shiny allover)</FONT>- and she doesn't like to wear a bra!||||reg||1
Z||000002||recluse||11-23-2001||06:06 PM||||I just put side scoops on my 87 GT today. (they look great!) I drilled out the rivets that hold the lower rocker panel on first. You might not have to take out the one closest to the front. There are 3 rivets on top  of the rocker under plastic tabs (open the door). I left the one closest to the front of the car in again.  Take out the small bolts that hold the plastic inner wheel whell.  Carefully pull the molding off (black molding at the top of the side panel).  I used a small pry bar wrapped around a rag.  Theres 3 or 4 rivets under there. 2 should hold on white plastic clips which hold the black molding on.  Drill out the rivets but dont damage the clips.  Then you have to move the panel around and try to pull everything back away from the car.  THeres 3 rivets that hold the panel onto the rocker, I took some wire cutters and cut the rivets off from the back side of the panel. I then had to take off the ground effect piece thats attatched to the side panel. Do this from the back side. Theres plastic studs with metal clips holding them on. I took a small screwdriver and needle nose pliars and bent the tabs up so i could pull them off without breaking anything.  I also had a small plastic rivet holding the panel on inside the door jam. After all that you should be able to pull the panel off.  Putting it back together I first reattatched the ground effect to the scoop panel with the metal clips and 2 rivets. (could use 3 but i only had 20. 30 should do the whole car, i just left some out of the rocker panel but will put some in later). Then with the rocker pulled back and away put the scoop on and rivet everything back together.  Sounds harder than it is, but it did take about an hour and a half for each side. The hardest part is drilling out the rivets because they like to spin. I took some pliars and held them in place while drilling. I used 6mm (for 1/4" holes) plastic rivets to put it all back together.  I got the gun $20 and rivets 20 for $6 at a NAPA that specalizes in paint and body work.  Hope this helps!||||reg||14
Z||000003||Zoom88||11-24-2001||12:00 PM||||Thanks Recluse,<P>    Good info. Who did you get your scoops from ?||||reg||10
